## 2. Configuring Qdrant for Dual Sparse and Dense Vectors

Qdrant supports storing and querying sparse and dense vector representations simultaneously within a single point record. This eliminates the need to run separate database instances for vector and keyword search.

### Initializing a Dual Sparse-Dense Collection in Qdrant

Send the following HTTP request to your Qdrant instance on Vultr VPS to create a collection configured for both dense embeddings (1536 dimensions) and sparse BM25 vectors:

```json
PUT /collections/enterprise_hybrid_knowledge
{
  "vectors": {
    "text-dense": {
      "size": 1536,
      "distance": "Cosine"
    }
  },
  "sparse_vectors": {
    "text-sparse": {
      "index": {
        "full_scan_threshold": 10000
      }
    }
  }
}
```

