## 4. Advanced BM25 Tokenization & Pre-Processing in n8n

Before sending sparse keyword vectors to Qdrant, input text strings must undergo tokenization, lowercasing, stop-word removal, and term-frequency hashing.

### JavaScript Text Pre-Processor Node for n8n

The following JavaScript code node converts raw search query strings into indexed sparse vectors formatted for Qdrant sparse search:

```javascript
// n8n Code Node: BM25 Sparse Vector Tokenizer & Frequency Hashing
const items = $input.all();
const STOP_WORDS = new Set(['the', 'a', 'an', 'and', 'or', 'in', 'on', 'at', 'to', 'for', 'of', 'with', 'is', 'it', 'by']);

function fnv1a32(str) {
  let hash = 0x811c9dc5;
  for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) {
    hash ^= str.charCodeAt(i);
    hash += (hash << 1) + (hash << 4) + (hash << 7) + (hash << 8) + (hash << 24);
  }
  return (hash >>> 0) % 2147483647; // Bounded positive 32-bit int index
}

return items.map((item) => {
  const query = item.json.body.query || '';
  const tokens = query.toLowerCase()
    .replace(/[^\w\s-]/g, '')
    .split(/\s+/)
    .filter(t => t.length > 1 && !STOP_WORDS.has(t));

  const termCounts = {};
  tokens.forEach(t => {
    termCounts[t] = (termCounts[t] || 0) + 1;
  });

  const indices = [];
  const values = [];

  Object.entries(termCounts).forEach(([term, count]) => {
    const idx = fnv1a32(term);
    const tf = Math.log(1 + count); // Log-scaled term frequency
    indices.push(idx);
    values.push(parseFloat(tf.toFixed(4)));
  });

  return {
    json: {
      query: query,
      sparse_indices: indices,
      sparse_values: values
    }
  };
});
```

